 ### Volume Fraction
-Volume Fraction is a specific variant of voxel occupancy determination where a cell is considered solid if the majority (or a specific cutoff value) of its volume is filled by the object [S2, unofficial]. This method requires calculating the volume of the intersection between the cube and the parametric surface to determine the fill ratio [S2, unofficial]. Alternatively, it can be approximated by choosing a representative or random set of points inside the cube, testing if they are inside the parametric object, and declaring the voxel occupied if a cutoff percentage of points are inside [S2, unofficial]. Binary Marching Cubes is described as a version of this method that specifically chooses the 8 corners of the cube as its test points and includes anti-aliasing [S2, unofficial]. Fractional occupancy varieties can use intermediate cases linked to other cutoff values as an anti-aliasing technique [S2, unofficial].
+Volume Fraction is a voxel occupancy determination method where a cell is considered solid if the majority (or a specific cutoff value) of its volume is filled by the object [S2, unofficial]. This method requires calculating the volume of the intersection between the cube and the parametric surface to determine the fill ratio [S2, unofficial]. Alternatively, it can be approximated by choosing a representative or random set of points inside the cube, testing if they are inside the parametric object, and declaring the voxel occupied if a cutoff percentage of points are inside [S2, unofficial]. Binary Marching Cubes is described as a version of this method that specifically chooses the 8 corners of the cube as its test points and includes anti-aliasing [S2, unofficial]. Fractional occupancy varieties can use intermediate cases linked to other cutoff values as an anti-aliasing technique [S2, unofficial].
 
